Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='nobackcompat', at=datetime(2026, 9, 25, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title='No backward compatibility, not even for data', body='*No backward compatibility, not even for data* (the owner, 2026-09-25: "no one outside of our usecase depends on our code"; 2026-10-01: "what\'s important is that we can always pull out an earlier checkpoint of the whole project"). Rename and delete freely and update every caller in the same series; no re-exports kept for importers, no deprecated aliases, no dual APIs, in Suzatary or the Prodrome. Stored data (chain objects, conversations, `state.json`, `instance.toml`) keeps reading until its format changes; a format change is an explicit migration verb, and once it has run on the box its verb, its reader of the old form and the old store are deleted, since the data repository\'s earlier commit holds the old data beside the code that read it (`docs/USERREPO-PLAN-2026-10-01.md` §2).', rationale='The owner, 2026-09-25: "no one outside of our usecase depends on our code"; and 2026-10-01: "what\'s important is that we can always pull out an earlier checkpoint of the whole project".', supersedes=()))